"en": "But system prompts aren't all-powerful.|Research tested twelve models:|'don't do X' prohibition constraints|saw compliance drop from 73% at turn five|to 33% at turn sixteen.|While 'do X' requirements barely declined.|In other words, the longer the conversation,|the more the model forgets what it shouldn't do.|Researchers call this phenomenon instruction forgetting.|That's why agents need more harness engineering.",
