      "summary": "Todo is not magic — it's a tool call in the agent runtime",
      "cn": "你可能会想，|就一个 todo list？|这也太简单了吧。|没错，是简单。|但关键是，它是怎么做到的？|答案是：它就是一个 tool call。|跟 agent 读文件、写代码一样，|操作 todo 也是调用一个工具。|agent 的运行时环境|会给它提供这些工具。",
      "en": "You might think:|just a todo list?|That's way too simple.|It is simple.|But the key question is, how does it work?|The answer: it's a tool call.|Just like reading files or writing code,|managing the todo is calling a tool.|The agent's runtime harness|provides these tools.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["tool call", "运行时环境"],
        "en": ["tool call", "runtime harness"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seg4-02",
      "summary": "The tool API: Create, Update, Read, and the status model",
      "cn": "具体来说，|一般会有这么几个操作。|首先是创建——|拿到任务的时候，|agent 调一次 TodoWrite 或 TaskCreate，|把计划写进去。|然后每做完一步，|调一次更新，|把状态从 pending 改成 completed。|还有读取——|每一轮循环开始的时候，|agent 先读一下 todo，|看看现在做到哪了。",
      "en": "Specifically,|there are a few operations.|First, create —|when the agent gets a task,|it calls TodoWrite or TaskCreate|to write the plan.|Then after each step,|it calls update|to change the status from pending to completed.|And there's read —|at the start of each loop,|the agent reads the todo|to see where things stand.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["TodoWrite", "TaskCreate", "读取"],
        "en": ["TodoWrite", "TaskCreate", "read"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seg4-03",
      "summary": "Constraints: one-in-progress + nag reminder prevents drift",
      "cn": "光有工具还不够。|还需要几条简单的规则。|比如同一时刻|只能有一个任务是 in progress——|这就逼着 agent 专注，|不能同时往好几个方向跑。|再比如，好几步都没看过 todo，|系统就会提醒它：|嘿，你是不是忘了看计划？|就这么两条，|就够防住大部分跑偏了。",
      "en": "Tools alone aren't enough.|You also need a few simple rules.|Only one task can be in progress at a time —|that forces the agent to focus,|it can't run in multiple directions.|And if several steps pass|without checking the todo,|the system nudges:|hey, did you forget the plan?|Just these two rules|prevent most drift.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["一个任务", "in progress", "提醒"],
        "en": ["one task", "in progress", "nudges"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seg4-04",
      "summary": "Cleanup: clear completed items to keep the list useful",
      "cn": "还有一个容易忽略的问题——|清理。|做了二十个步骤，|清单上全是 completed，|有用的信息反而被淹没了。|所以好的 todo 系统|会定期清理已完成的条目，|只留下还在进行的和待做的。|保持清单简洁，|才能让 agent 一眼看到重点。",
      "en": "There's one more thing people overlook —|cleanup.|After twenty steps,|the list is full of completed items,|and the useful info gets buried.|A good todo system|periodically clears completed entries,|keeping only in-progress and pending.|A clean list|lets the agent see what matters at a glance.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["清理", "保持清单简洁"],
        "en": ["cleanup", "clean list"]
      }
    }
  ]
},
{
  "id": "seg5",
  "title": "不同平台，同一个思路",
  "targetDurationSeconds": 35,
  "narrativeRoute": "platform differences → shared pattern → closing insight → bridge to hooks",
  "visualPhases": [
    "不同平台的 todo 工具名称对比",
    "共同的模式：外部状态 + 结构化 + 随时可读",
    "总结：不是更聪明的模型，而是更好的记忆",
