      "summary": "The tool parameters: an array of {id, content, status} objects + merge flag",
      "cn": "具体怎么调呢？|TodoWrite 接收一个 JSON 数组，|每一项有三个字段：|id，唯一标识；|content，任务内容；|status，就是 pending、in_progress、completed 三选一。|还有一个 merge 参数——|如果是 true，就把新的 todo 合并进已有的清单；|如果是 false，就用新的替换掉旧的。|就这么简单，没有别的了。",
      "en": "How exactly?|TodoWrite takes a JSON array.|Each item has three fields:|id, a unique identifier;|content, the task description;|status — pending, in_progress, or completed.|There's also a merge flag —|true merges into the existing list,|false replaces it entirely.|That's it, nothing else.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["id", "content", "status", "merge"],
        "en": ["id", "content", "status", "merge"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seg4-03",
      "summary": "Where it's stored and how it gets back into context — outside messages, injected every turn",
      "cn": "关键在于它的数据存在哪。|agent 调完 TodoWrite 之后，|runtime 会把这个 JSON|存到对话消息之外的一块独立区域。|然后每一轮对话开始的时候，|runtime 会把最新的 todo 状态|重新注入到上下文里。|所以不管对话怎么被压缩，|todo 每次都是完整的、最新的。|这就是它不会被吃掉的原因。",
      "en": "The key is where the data lives.|After the agent calls TodoWrite,|the runtime stores that JSON|in a separate area, outside the conversation messages.|Then at the start of each turn,|the runtime re-injects|the latest todo state back into the context.|So no matter how the conversation gets compressed,|the todo is always complete and up-to-date.|That's why it doesn't get swallowed.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["独立区域", "重新注入", "不会被吃掉"],
        "en": ["separate area", "re-injects", "doesn't get swallowed"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seg4-04",
      "summary": "System prompt rules: one-in-progress, nag injection, cleanup",
      "cn": "但光有工具不够。|系统提示词里还写了几条使用规则。|第一条：同一时刻只能有一个任务是 in progress。|这条不是工具层面的硬限制，|是写在 system prompt 里的软约束——|模型看到了就会遵守。|第二条：如果好几步都没更新过 todo，|runtime 会往上下文里注入一条提醒：|你是不是忘了看计划？|第三条：todo 超过二十条的时候，|清理掉已完成的，只留活跃的。|就这几条规则，|配上一个简单的工具，|就够用了。",
      "en": "But the tool alone isn't enough.|The system prompt adds a few usage rules.|Rule one: only one task can be in_progress at a time.|This isn't a hard limit in the tool —|it's a soft constraint written in the system prompt.|The model sees it and follows it.|Rule two: if several steps pass without updating the todo,|the runtime injects a reminder into the context:|did you forget to check the plan?|Rule three: when the list exceeds twenty items,|clear completed ones, keep only active tasks.|Just these few rules,|paired with a simple tool,|and it works.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["system prompt", "软约束", "注入一条提醒", "清理"],
        "en": ["system prompt", "soft constraint", "injects a reminder", "clear"]
      }
    }
  ]
},
{
  "id": "seg5",
  "title": "不同平台，同一个套路",
  "targetDurationSeconds": 40,
  "narrativeRoute": "Claude Code TodoWrite → Tasks 升级 → Cursor → Codex → 外部状态本质 → bridge to hooks",
  "visualPhases": [
    "Claude Code: TodoWrite → Tasks 升级路径",
    "Cursor 和 Codex 的做法",
    "核心本质：外部化的结构化状态",
    "预告 Hooks"
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "id": "seg5-01",
      "summary": "Claude Code's evolution: TodoWrite → Tasks with persistence and multi-agent support",
      "cn": "各家产品的做法大同小异。|Claude Code 一开始就是 TodoWrite，|session 级别的，关了就没了。|后来他们做了一次升级，|换成了 Tasks 系统——|TaskCreate、TaskUpdate、TaskGet、TaskList，|四个独立的工具。|最大的变化是|任务可以存到磁盘上了，|关掉会话再打开还在。|而且多个 agent 可以共享同一个任务列表，|协同工作。",
      "en": "Each platform does it slightly differently.|Claude Code started with TodoWrite —|session-level, gone when you close.|Then they upgraded|to a Tasks system —|TaskCreate, TaskUpdate, TaskGet, TaskList,|four separate tools.|The biggest change:|tasks now persist to disk.|Close the session, reopen, they're still there.|And multiple agents|can share the same task list|and work together.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["TaskCreate", "TaskUpdate", "存到磁盘", "共享"],
        "en": ["TaskCreate", "TaskUpdate", "persist to disk", "share"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seg5-02",
      "summary": "Cursor and Codex: same pattern, different surface",
      "cn": "Cursor 也有自己的 TodoWrite，|用法差不多，也是 session 级别的。|Codex 走的路不太一样，|它是内置的任务追踪，|agent 做事的时候自动生成和更新，|不需要显式调工具。|但不管表面怎么不同，|底层的思路是一模一样的——|给 agent 一块不会被对话吞掉的地方，|放它的工作状态。",
      "en": "Cursor has its own TodoWrite,|similar usage, also session-scoped.|Codex takes a different approach —|built-in task tracking|that auto-generates and updates|without explicit tool calls.|But no matter how the surface differs,|the underlying idea is identical —|give the agent a place|that won't get swallowed by the conversation|to store its working state.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["Cursor", "Codex", "不会被对话吞掉"],
        "en": ["Cursor", "Codex", "won't get swallowed"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seg5-03",
      "summary": "Core insight: todo = externalized state. Closing + hooks bridge",
      "cn": "说到底，|todo 就是 agent 的外部化状态。|对话是流动的，|会被压缩、被截断、被遗忘。|但 todo 不会。|你不需要更聪明的模型。|你只需要给它一块|不会随着对话消失的记忆。|下一集我们讲 Hooks——|有了计划之后，|执行的时候怎么在关键节点|停下来检查。|我们下集见。",
      "en": "At the end of the day,|the todo is the agent's externalized state.|Conversations flow —|they get compressed, truncated, forgotten.|But the todo doesn't.|You don't need a smarter model.|You just need to give it|a piece of memory that doesn't disappear with the conversation.|Next episode: Hooks —|once you have a plan,|how do you stop and check|at critical points during execution?|See you next time.",
      "highlights": {
        "cn": ["外部化状态", "不会随着对话消失"],
        "en": ["externalized state", "doesn't disappear"]
      }
    }
  ]
}

