          "en": "The core of the permission system is three rules —|deny, ask, and allow.|Deny means forbidden.|Regardless of the reason,|this operation cannot execute.|For example, you can set a rule:|deny git push.|No matter how the agent reasons or requests,|push operations are always blocked.|Ask means confirmation required.|The agent wants to execute this operation,|but must ask you first.|You see the exact command,|then decide to approve or reject.|Allow means auto-approve.|Safe operations like reading files or running tests|don't need to ask every time.",
