          "summary": "Cursor: sandbox with workspace-only access. Codex: container with network off by default. Common ground: reads free, writes restricted.",
          "cn": "Cursor 走的是沙箱路线。|Agent 执行的命令|默认跑在一个受限的沙箱里——|只能读写项目目录和临时文件夹，|不能访问网络。|你可以设置一个命令白名单，|白名单上的命令|跳过沙箱直接执行。|Codex 更激进——|默认关闭网络。|agent 跑在一个容器里，|写操作限制在工作区内，|.git 目录只读。|它把安全性内建在运行环境里，|而不只是靠规则。|三家的共同点是：|读操作基本自由，|写操作默认受限，|危险操作都需要额外控制。",
          "en": "Cursor takes a sandbox approach.|Commands the agent runs|default to a restricted sandbox —|only workspace directory and temp folder access,|no network.|You can set a command allowlist|where listed commands|bypass the sandbox.|Codex goes further —|network is off by default.|The agent runs in a container|with writes limited to the workspace,|.git directory read-only.|It builds safety into the runtime environment,|not just rules.|What all three share:|reads are mostly free,|writes are restricted by default,|and dangerous operations all need extra controls.",
