          "en": "The permission system isn't a single switch —|it's multiple defense layers stacked together.|Layer one is system prompt —|covered in episode two.|It tells the agent|don't push to main.|But prompts are just suggestions —|the model might not listen.|Layer two is tool-level permissions —|the deny, ask, allow rules we just discussed.|This is real execution-level control.|Layer three is path sandboxing.|Restricting the agent to project directories only —|no reading .env files,|no modifying .git config,|no touching system files.",
          "highlights": {
            "cn": ["系统提示词", "工具级权限", "路径沙箱"],
            "en": ["system prompt", "tool-level permissions", "path sandboxing"]
