          "en": "Layer four is hooks —|covered in episode four.|You can write a PreToolUse hook|that runs custom checks before every tool call.|Like scanning commands for secrets|or blocking commits to specific branches.|Layer five is human confirmation.|The agent shows you a dialog|with the full operation details,|and you click approve or reject.|Layer six is container isolation —|the Codex approach.|The agent runs in an isolated container,|so even if it tries to cause damage,|the operating system won't let it.|Six defense layers, each catching a portion of risks.|The deeper you go, the harder they are —|prompts can be ignored,|but container isolation can't be bypassed by the agent.",
          "highlights": {
            "cn": ["hooks", "人工确认", "容器隔离", "六层防线"],
            "en": ["hooks", "human confirmation", "container isolation", "Six defense layers"]
